# grammar the curriculum deliberately does not drill, and why.
#
# the mirror of learn/skip, for learn/syntax. every row of that table is
# either DECLARED by a level's syntax: header -- and required by a block of
# that same level, so the declaration cannot be a lie -- or listed here with
# a reason. selftest fails on anything in neither.
#
# the row stays in learn/syntax either way. the reference panel must still
# explain a construct the learner meets in a script, even one no card drills;
# retiring it here retires the DRILL, not the explanation.
#
# format:  <label>   # reason
#
# the whole line before the # is the label, because labels carry spaces:
# `[ ]`, `{ }`, `( )`, `$1..$9`. there is no second field to get wrong.
#
# the reasons, closed the way lib/lint's why: list is closed:
#   multiline    -- cannot be written on the one line an answer is
#   interactive  -- only meaningful at a live prompt, never inside sh -c
#   redundant    -- a second spelling of a construct a card already drills
#   pending      -- drillable and owed a card; the commit that teaches it
#                   deletes this line. same promise as learn/skip's pending.

<<              # multiline -- a heredoc needs its body on the next line, and an answer is one line

( )             # pending
{ }             # pending
$@              # pending
$*              # pending
$#              # pending
$0              # pending
$1..$9          # pending
${NAME#%}       # pending
`CMD`           # pending
[...]           # pending
?               # pending
~               # pending
--              # pending
